  "period_note": "Balance sheet is the period-end snapshot (reported) as at 30 June 2025, from Midland Bank's own genuinely-filed, BSEC/DSE/CSE-submitted quarterly financial statements (Un-Audited). Income-statement items are CUMULATIVE from 1 January 2025 (1 January to 30 June 2025), flagged via the _cumulative suffix. SOLO / STANDALONE basis -- 'Midland Bank PLC.' / 'Midland Bank Limited' single-entity statements, distinct from the Consolidated statements the bank has also prepared since Q1 2024 (covering its subsidiary Midland Bank Asset Management Company Ltd., BSEC-licensed 4 August 2024); this file uses only the Solo figures, matching the bank's main annual Q4 series basis. provision_charge_cumulative and tax_expense_cumulative are the report's own printed 'Total Provision' and 'Provision for Tax' lines (reported, not calculated, unlike the annual Q4 series which has to derive these because its summary table omits them). 'Half-Yearly' filing used as the Q2 data point. A 3% bonus share issue (191,900,920 BDT face value) was recorded during this quarter, taking paid-up capital from 6,396,697,530 to 6,588,598,450 and shares outstanding from 639,669,753 to 658,859,845; NAV per share here (14.56) uses the new post-bonus share count and matches the FY2025 annual report's own 30-Jun-25 NAV figure exactly. DISCREPANCY FOUND (contemporaneous figure kept, divergence recorded per project policy): this bank's own later 'Financial-Statements-Q2-2026.pdf' filing shows its comparative column for the SAME period ('01 January 2025 to 30 June 2025') with net_interest_income reported as +382,129,180 (not -405,169,535) and combined investment/commission/other income as 1,648,924,468 (not 2,436,223,184) -- i.e. roughly 787m BDT of income reclassified from the investment-income line into net interest income between when this report was originally filed (~July 2025) and when it was next shown as a prior-year comparative (~August 2026). Total Operating Income is IDENTICAL either way (2,031,053,649), so this is a presentation reclassification between interest and investment income, not a restatement of profit. This record keeps the figures as originally filed in this bank's own Q2 2025 report (the contemporaneous source), per this dataset's standing rule to prefer contemporaneous figures over later restated comparatives. For comparison, Q1 2025 and Q3 2025 show NO such divergence -- their own P&L figures reproduce exactly in both the Q1-2026 and the FY2025 annual report's tables, so this reclassification appears isolated to the Apr-Jun 2025 discrete quarter specifically, not a blanket policy change applied retroactively to the whole year.",
